.Dd February 14, 2026
.Dt VOP_SYMLINK 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm VOP_SYMLINK
.Nd create a symbolic link
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_SYMLINK "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap" "const char *target"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn VOP_SYMLINK
entry point creates a symbolic link in a directory.
.Pp
The arguments are:
.Bl -tag -width target
.It Fa dvp
The vnode of the directory in which to create the symbolic link.
.It Fa vpp
Return location for the vnode of the created symbolic link.
.It Fa cnp
Pathname component information for the link name.
.It Fa vap
Attributes for the new symbolic link (e.g. modes).
.It Fa target
The target path string for the symbolic link.
.El
.Sh LOCKS
The directory
.Fa dvp
should be locked on entry and remains locked on return.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero is returned on success, otherwise an error code is returned.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width EOPNOTSUPP
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The file system does not support creating symbolic links.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The argument
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
The name already exists.
.It Bq Er ENOSPC
The file system is full.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr VOP_READLINK 9
